stimulus.description:
A student is writing a class DigitTools with two static methods that work with the digits of a positive integer.
```java
public class DigitTools {
    /** Returns the sum of the digits of n. Precondition: n >= 0. */
    public static int digitSum(int n) { /* part (a) */ }

    /** Returns the smallest integer that is greater than or equal to start and is divisible by its own digit sum.
     *  Precondition: start >= 1. */
    public static int firstHarshad(int start) { /* part (b) */ }
}
```

parts.model_answer:
One correct implementation (ALTON reference answer):
```java
    public static int digitSum(int n) {
        int sum = 0;
        while (n > 0) {
            sum += n % 10;
            n /= 10;
        }
        return sum;
    }
```

One correct implementation (ALTON reference answer):
```java
    public static int firstHarshad(int start) {
        int k = start;
        while (k % digitSum(k) != 0) {
            k++;
        }
        return k;
    }
```

